    "turn": 2,
    "user": "Nice, thanks 🙂 Which part do people usually get wrong?",
    "response": "You're welcome! 😊\n\nPeople often get confused about **the purpose of the Jacobian determinant** when changing variables in multiple integrals. Specifically, they might not fully grasp why we need to multiply by the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant — it's because it accounts for how the transformation stretches or compresses space, and we need to adjust the volume accordingly.\n\nAlso, people sometimes mix up the **Jacobian matrix** (the full matrix of partial derivatives) and the **Jacobian determinant** (its determinant). It's important to remember that the determinant is just one part of the story — especially when doing substitutions in integrals.",
